WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.390
Use one antibiotic again and again,
and resistant bacteria take over.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.950
Selection pushes, and the
whole population shifts,

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.410
generation after generation.

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.400
Keep that up for long enough, and you
might expect every trait to keep moving

5
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.590
one way.

6
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.210
So why doesn't selection always push
a population in the same direction?

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.760
In this mission, you'll read
evidence from real populations,

8
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.450
studied in the wild or in hospitals.

9
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.490
Then you'll predict which
way a trait will move next,

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.190
and explain why.

11
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.060
Your mission: explain why selection doesn't
always push a population in the same

12
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:37.880
direction.
